-- #15: Karnataka Chitrakala Parishath (Bengaluru, Karnataka)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'Karnataka Chitrakala Parishath, located on Kumara Krupa Road in Bengaluru, is a premier visual art institution and museum complex established in 1960. The complex houses multiple permanent galleries displaying significant collections of traditional, folk, modern, and contemporary Indian art. The institution is renowned for holding the largest collection of paintings by the master Russian artist Nicholas Roerich and his son Svetoslav Roerich, capturing breathtaking Himalayan landscapes and spiritual portraiture. Other major highlights include rare traditional Mysore gold foil paintings, historical leather puppets (Togalu Gombeyaata), indigenous folk crafts, and sculptures from across Karnataka. The campus also hosts the annual Chitra Santhe, one of India''s largest public art fairs, bringing together hundreds of thousands of artists and art lovers. The Parishath serves as a vibrant cultural nexus nurturing artistic education and heritage appreciation in South India.'
