-- #16: Visvesvaraya Industrial and Technological Museum (Bengaluru, Karnataka)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The Visvesvaraya Industrial and Technological Museum, located in Kasturba Road adjacent to Cubbon Park in Bengaluru, was inaugurated in 1965 in honor of Bharat Ratna Sir M. Visvesvaraya. Operated by the National Council of Science Museums, it is one of South India''s most popular interactive science centres. Across multiple floors, visitors engage with interactive exhibits exploring mechanical engineering, electronics, aerospace technology, biotechnology, and space exploration. Key attractions include the Engine Hall showcasing working internal combustion engines, an interactive Dinosaur Corner with a moving animatronic Spinosaurus, a full-scale replica of the 1903 Wright Brothers flyer, and the Fun Science gallery where physics principles come alive through play. The museum conducts live 3D shows, Taramandal planetarium presentations, and science workshops, making it a beloved educational hub for inquisitive learners of all ages.'
