-- #18: HAL Aerospace Museum (Bengaluru, Karnataka)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The HAL Aerospace Museum, established in 2001 by Hindustan Aeronautics Limited on Old Airport Road in Bengaluru, is India''s first dedicated aerospace museum. Spanning four acres of landscaped grounds, the museum celebrates the nation''s indigenous aeronautical engineering milestones and industrial defense heritage. Outdoor display zones feature real decommissioned military and civilian aircraft, including the iconic HF-24 Marut (India''s first indigenous fighter-bomber), the Kiran jet trainer, MiG-21, Sea Harrier, Ajeet, and the advanced Dhruv helicopter. Indoor galleries display detailed engine cutaways illustrating the evolution of piston and jet turbines, pilot survival gear, avionics systems, and archival photographs of India''s aviation pioneers. Motion flight simulators allow visitors to experience piloting combat aircraft, while a mock Air Traffic Control tower provides panoramic views over the facility, making it a thrilling destination for aviation enthusiasts.'
