-- #19: Albert Hall Museum (Jaipur, Rajasthan)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The Albert Hall Museum, standing majestically within the Ram Niwas Garden in Jaipur, is the oldest museum in Rajasthan and the state''s official museum of art and history. Commissioned during the royal visit of the Prince of Wales in 1876 and designed by Sir Samuel Swinton Jacob, the building is an exceptional architectural masterpiece of the Indo-Saracenic style, adorned with intricately carved stone arches, domes, and open courtyards. The museum houses a splendid and eclectic collection of art objects from Rajasthan and around the globe. Notable exhibits include an authentic Egyptian mummy from the Ptolemaic era, celebrated Persian garden carpets, delicate miniature paintings from the Jaipur, Mewar, and Bundi schools, brass ware, musical instruments, marble statues, ivory carvings, and royal armaments. Lit up dramatically at night, Albert Hall remains a premier symbol of Jaipur''s rich cultural elegance.'
