-- #20: City Palace Museum, Jaipur (Jaipur, Rajasthan)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The City Palace Museum, formally known as the Maharaja Sawai Man Singh II Museum, is situated within the historic City Palace complex in the heart of Jaipur''s walled city. Built by Maharaja Sawai Jai Singh II and expanded by successive rulers, the palace showcases an exquisite blend of Rajput, Mughal, and European architecture. The museum holds the priceless royal heirlooms of the Kachwaha dynasty. Highlights include the Mubarak Mahal textile gallery, displaying ornate royal costumes, pashmina shawls, and polo uniforms; the Sileh Khana armoury, exhibiting an extraordinary collection of Rajput and Mughal swords, shields, and matchlocks; and the Sabha Niwas banquet hall. In the Sarvato Bhadra courtyard stand two colossal sterling silver urns, officially recorded in the Guinness World Records as the world''s largest silver vessels, used to carry sacred Ganga water abroad.'
