-- #21: Rajasthan State Museum (Jaipur, Rajasthan)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The Rajasthan State Museum, operating under the Directorate of Archaeology and Museums of the Government of Rajasthan in Jaipur, functions as the central custodian of archaeological discoveries and regional historical artefacts from across Rajasthan. The museum preserves extensive antiquities excavated from ancient archaeological sites, ranging from Bronze Age civilizations to medieval fortresses. Its collections include finely carved Gurjara-Pratihara and Chahamana stone sculptures, ancient inscriptions, coins of various Rajput kingdoms, regional folk art, traditional weapons, and textiles representing the distinct cultural regions of Marwar, Mewar, Shekhawati, and Hadoti. Informative curated galleries illustrate the strategic fort architecture, dynastic lineages, and rich artisanal traditions that defined the royal states of Rajputana. The museum provides researchers and travelers with an authoritative overview of Rajasthan''s archaeological heritage and cultural evolution.'
