-- #22: Calico Museum of Textiles (Ahmedabad, Gujarat)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The Calico Museum of Textiles in Ahmedabad is widely recognized as one of the world''s finest museums devoted to historic Indian fabrics and decorative weaving. Founded in 1949 by Gautam and Gira Sarabhai and housed within the serene heritage retreat of the Sarabhai Foundation in Shahibag, the museum is renowned for its scholarly curation and conservation standards. Its extraordinary collection encompasses five centuries of Indian textile artistry. Masterpieces on view include Mughal court textiles, intricate Gujarati Patola double-ikat weaves, hand-painted Kalamkari temple hangings, Pichhwai tapestries from Nathdwara, royal Kashmiri shawls, and regional tribal embroideries. The museum also displays bronze sculptures, Jain manuscripts, and historic wooden architecture. Preserving the supreme craftsmanship of Indian weavers and dyers, the Calico Museum stands as an internationally celebrated center of textile design and historic research.'
