-- #23: Vikram Sarabhai Space Exhibition (Ahmedabad, Gujarat)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The Vikram Sarabhai Space Exhibition, located at the Space Applications Centre of the Indian Space Research Organisation (ISRO) in Ahmedabad, is dedicated to inspiring the public about India''s achievements in space exploration. Named in honor of Dr. Vikram Sarabhai, the visionary father of the Indian space programme, the exhibition offers a captivating look into satellite technology and launch operations. Visitors can view full-scale and precision scale models of major Indian rockets including the PSLV and GSLV, as well as planetary probes like Chandrayaan and Mangalyaan. Interactive touchscreens, informative video presentations, and working mock-ups explain how space-based remote sensing, weather forecasting, and telecommunications benefit national development. With dedicated 3D theatres and educational zones, the centre provides an engaging scientific experience for students and space enthusiasts interested in India''s cosmic frontiers.'
