-- #24: Varanasi Museum (Varanasi, Uttar Pradesh)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The Varanasi Museum collection, anchored by the renowned Bharat Kala Bhavan university museum at Banaras Hindu University, is an internationally acclaimed repository of Indian art, archaeology, and literature. Situated in the ancient city of Varanasi, the museum reflects the profound spiritual, artistic, and intellectual legacy of the sacred Ganges river basin. The museum is especially famous for its magnificent collection of Mughal, Rajasthani, and Pahari miniature paintings, as well as illustrated Jain manuscripts and palm-leaf scriptures. Archaeological galleries display rare Gupta and Maurya stone sculptures, exquisite terracottas from Rajghat, historic Banarasi brocades and Zari silks, and a unique literary gallery preserving personal letters and original manuscripts of eminent Hindi and Urdu writers. For scholars and travelers, the museum offers an irreplaceable window into the artistic genius of classical and medieval India.'
