-- #25: Allahabad Museum (Prayagraj, Uttar Pradesh)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The Allahabad Museum, located inside the historic Chandrashekhar Azad Park in Prayagraj, is a premier national-level museum under the Ministry of Culture, Government of India. Celebrated for its rich multidisciplinary holdings, the museum preserves exceptional archaeological collections, including early Buddhist stone sculptures from Bharhut, Kaushambi terracottas, and carved panels from medieval temples. The museum holds deep significance for India''s freedom struggle; here, visitors can view the original Colt pistol of revolutionary hero Chandrashekhar Azad and the Gandhi Smriti Vahan, the vehicle used to carry Mahatma Gandhi''s ashes to the Sangam in 1948. Additionally, the museum houses the personal archives, photographs, and manuscripts of renowned literary figures like Sumitranandan Pant and Mahadevi Varma, alongside galleries of decorative arts, miniature paintings, and modern Indian art, serving as a vital cultural institution of Northern India.'
