-- #26: Lucknow Museum (Lucknow, Uttar Pradesh)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The Lucknow Museum, officially known as the State Museum Lucknow, was established in 1863 and is one of the oldest and largest regional state museums in India. Situated in the lush grounds of the Prince of Wales Zoological Gardens in Banarasi Bagh, Lucknow, the museum holds over one hundred thousand antiquities spanning archaeology, numismatics, epigraphy, and fine arts. Its archaeological wing is celebrated for housing magnificent Kushana and Gupta stone sculptures from Mathura, early Jain Ayagapatas, and medieval bronzes. A major attraction for visitors is an authentic three-thousand-year-old Egyptian mummy displayed in an Egyptian gallery. Other galleries exhibit the refined courtly culture of the Nawabs of Awadh, including royal silver, embroidered Chikan garments, miniature paintings, and antique weapons. The museum stands as a monumental storehouse of Uttar Pradesh''s deep historical and artistic heritage.'
