-- #27: Kanpur Museum (Kanpur, Uttar Pradesh)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The Kanpur Museum, also known as the Kanpur Sangrahalaya, is located at Phool Bagh in the historic heart of Kanpur. Housed in a grand colonial-era building originally constructed as the King Edward Memorial Hall, the museum chronicles the multifaceted history of Kanpur from its ancient settlements and dramatic role in the 1857 Indian Uprising to its rise as a leading industrial textile center of North India. The exhibits include rare historical photographs, colonial documents, and personal artefacts associated with legendary freedom fighters including Nana Saheb Peshwa, Tatya Tope, and Rani Lakshmibai. Visitors can explore displays of antique artillery, muskets, uniforms, prehistoric stone implements, and regional archaeological finds. By narrating the dramatic transformation of the city from nineteenth-century Cawnpore into modern Kanpur, the museum serves as an indispensable institution for regional history.'
