-- #29: Victoria Jubilee Museum (Vijayawada, Andhra Pradesh)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The Victoria Jubilee Museum, modernized as the Bapu Museum, is a prestigious archaeological museum located on B. G. R. Road in Vijayawada, Andhra Pradesh. Originally constructed in 1887 to commemorate the Golden Jubilee of Queen Victoria, the grand heritage building has been integrated with contemporary interactive galleries honoring the renowned Telugu artist, filmmaker, and illustrator Bapu. The museum preserves a remarkable collection of ancient stone sculptures from the Satavahana, Ikshvaku, Eastern Chalukya, and Vijayanagara periods, alongside prehistoric microlithic tools, bronzes, porcelain, and royal weaponry. The site holds immense historical significance: it was here in 1921, during the All India Congress Committee meeting, that Pingali Venkayya presented the tricolor national flag design to Mahatma Gandhi. Through state-of-the-art digital displays and rare antiquities, the museum vividly narrates the cultural evolution of Andhra Pradesh.'
