-- #30: Visakha Museum (Visakhapatnam, Andhra Pradesh)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The Visakha Museum, also known as the Corporation Museum, is situated in a charmingly restored Dutch colonial bungalow along the scenic Beach Road in Visakhapatnam. Established to preserve the maritime, cultural, and military history of the coastal city and the Northern Circars region, the museum houses a captivating array of antiquities and naval memorabilia. Notable exhibits include authentic artillery pieces, torpedo models, deep-sea diving gear, and artefacts salvaged from the Pakistani submarine PNS Ghazi, which sank off the coast of Visakhapatnam during the 1971 Indo-Pak war. Cultural galleries display royal portraits and regal heirlooms of the Bobbili and Vizianagaram dynasties, prehistoric stone implements, ancient coins, traditional wooden musical instruments, and historical photographs capturing the city''s transformation into a major seaport. It offers visitors a compelling tribute to coastal Andhra''s naval defense and local heritage.'
WHERE id = 30;

-- #31: Archaeological Site Museum, Nagarjunakonda (Nagarjunakonda, Andhra Pradesh)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The Archaeological Site Museum at Nagarjunakonda is a unique island museum set in the picturesque waters of the Nagarjuna Sagar reservoir in Andhra Pradesh. When the Krishna River was dammed in the 1950s, the Archaeological Survey of India undertook an unprecedented salvage excavation, relocating monumental Buddhist stupas, monasteries, and sculptures to this elevated island plateau. The museum showcases the exquisite artistic and intellectual achievements of ancient Vijayapuri, the prosperous capital of the Ikshvaku dynasty in the third and fourth centuries CE. Visitors can admire magnificent white limestone carvings illustrating Buddhist narratives, life-sized statues of Gautama Buddha, Roman gold coins testifying to vibrant maritime commerce, and detailed architectural models of the excavated monastic complexes. Named after the revered Mahayana philosopher Acharya Nagarjuna, this island sanctuary offers an unforgettable journey into India''s early Buddhist heritage.'
WHERE id = 31;

-- #32: Jawaharlal Nehru Museum, Itanagar (Itanagar, Arunachal Pradesh)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The Jawaharlal Nehru State Museum in Itanagar is the premier ethnographic museum of Arunachal Pradesh, dedicated to preserving and celebrating the cultural heritage of the state''s diverse indigenous tribes. Established in the late twentieth century, the museum features two spacious floors of curated galleries that offer an authentic glimpse into the daily life, traditions, and belief systems of communities such as the Nyishi, Apatani, Monpa, Adi, and Tagin. The ground floor displays a colorful collection of tribal textiles, elaborate headgear adorned with hornbill beaks, cane and bamboo craftwork, hunting weapons, and ceremonial ornaments. The upper floor exhibits archaeological discoveries unearthed from historical sites such as Ita Fort, Malinithan, and Nokparbat, alongside traditional musical instruments and woodcarvings. The museum provides an essential orientation for understanding the tribal heritage of the Eastern Himalayas.'
