-- #33: Craft Museum and Emporium (Itanagar, Arunachal Pradesh)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The Craft Museum and Emporium in Itanagar serves as a vital showcase for the exceptional artisanal traditions and living crafts of Arunachal Pradesh. Operated to support indigenous tribal artisans, the museum highlights the intricate material culture developed across the diverse valleys of the frontier state. The exhibits feature traditional handloom textiles woven on loin looms, vibrant Monpa wool carpets, Buddhist thangka scroll paintings, delicate silver filigree ornaments, wooden masks used in monastic dances, and masterfully woven bamboo and cane baskets. Visitors can observe craft demonstrations illustrating ancient spinning, weaving, and woodcarving techniques handed down through generations. An adjoining government emporium allows visitors to acquire authentic tribal handicrafts directly from artisan cooperatives, promoting economic sustainability while preserving the ancestral aesthetic traditions of Arunachal Pradesh''s mountain communities.'
