-- #34: Assam State Museum (Guwahati, Assam)
UPDATE museums
SET description = 'The Assam State Museum, located on the southern bank of the historic Dighalipukhuri tank in Guwahati, is the premier cultural institution of Northeast India. Established in 1940 by the Kamarupa Anusandhan Samiti (Assam Research Society), the museum preserves an invaluable collection representing the archaeological, ethnographic, and natural heritage of the Brahmaputra valley. Its archaeological wing displays ancient stone sculptures and epigraphs from the early medieval Kamarupa kingdom, notably artefacts excavated from Ambari, alongside ancient copper-plate charters and terracotta tablets. Visitors can view historical arms and massive cannons used during the legendary Ahom kingdom''s resistance against Mughal expansion, royal garments, traditional musical instruments, and ethnographic displays of regional tribes like the Bodo, Mishing, and Karbi. The museum remains an indispensable destination for exploring the rich historical narrative of Assam.'
